deep within the waters of Mexico's  Yucatan Peninsula is a cavern called oil  negra the name means black hole which is  fitting because it is a lightless void  about the size of a professional  basketball arena when the region was dry  before about 10,000 years ago a sinkhole  that fed into oil may grow swallowed up  a collection of saber-toothed cats giant  ground sloths mammoths and even a young  girl the human skeletons slight build  relatively wide pelvis and incomplete  tooth development indicated that it came  from a 15 to 16 year old girl who the  divers name nya which means water nymph  analysis of the girls skeleton revealed  that she stood four feet ten inches tall  radiocarbon dating of one of nice teeth  and analyses of calcite deposits that  formed on her bones after she fell into  the cave suggested that the youth had  lived 12,000 to 13,000 years ago in  March 2014 divers on the research team  returned to retrieve nya skull and four  additional bones like other ancient  American skulls knives facial features  differ from those of modern Native  Americans but analysis of DNA from one  of her teeth shows that the girl carried  in Asian derived set of gene variants  previously found only in North and South  America the analysis also shows that the  ancient youth and modern Native  Americans share a genetic profile that  probably evolved between twenty six  thousand and eighteen thousand years ago  the results appear May sixteenth in  science
 

